# Caddy: HTTPS in front of the api container. WebSocket upgrades (/ws) pass
# through reverse_proxy automatically.
#
# SITE ADDRESS: 203.0.113.10 is a placeholder documentation IP. Replace it with
# the server's real address (README "Where to put the AWS address"), keeping it
# identical to PUBLIC_BASE_URL in server/.env.
#
# Production: use a DOMAIN NAME here (e.g. eruv.example.org) and delete the
# "tls internal" line. Caddy then gets a public Let's Encrypt certificate by
# itself (ports 80 and 443 must be open). iOS release builds and the Pi agent
# require a publicly trusted certificate.
#
# Development on a bare IP: a public CA will normally not issue a certificate
# for a bare IP, so "tls internal" makes Caddy sign one with its own local CA.
# Phones and the Pi do not trust that CA; see docs/runbook.md "Development on
# a bare IP" for the plain-HTTP alternative.

203.0.113.10 {
	tls internal

	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy api:8000
}
